          'The platform navigation is organized into logical module groups accessible from the left sidebar. Each group represents a functional area of the platform and contains related modules. Understanding this organizational structure will help you locate the tools and information you need efficiently. The sidebar can be collapsed to icon-only mode to maximize the content area, and expanded again by clicking the menu toggle button.',
          'The Core Management section is the primary area for day-to-day identity and access administration. It includes the following modules: Dashboard (governance posture overview with KPIs and trend charts), Responsibilities (ownership and delegation management for governance accountability), Applications (connected system management with connector configuration and health monitoring), Identities (comprehensive identity management across human, non-human, and non-employee types), Identity Groups (static and dynamic group management for bulk governance operations), Access Catalog (centralized repository of all roles and entitlements available for request), Organizations (organizational hierarchy management for governance scoping), and Lifecycle Management (JML workflow configuration and lifecycle event tracking).',
